+// STRATA_ADAPT_GATE=1 (fork, opt-in; from Hardin22/Strata-DualGPU bce7fbb3): true while a verify window's CPU expert
+// pool runs (drive_pool_multi).  The asynchronous adaptive tier's host copies (the bounce reads of pageable experts,
+// the RAM side of the exchanges) wait while it is set, so they take RAM bandwidth while the host waits for the GPU -
+// most of a window - and not from the pool, which is bound by it.  Unset: never set, nothing waits.
+bool adapt_gate_on() {
+    static const bool on = [] { const char* v = std::getenv("STRATA_ADAPT_GATE"); return v != nullptr && std::atoi(v) != 0; }();
